00:13:43.783 --> 00:13:45.123
- Dory!
- Hello?

239
00:13:45.284 --> 00:13:47.624
- Dory!
- Ah! Where did you go?

240
00:13:48.704 --> 00:13:50.985
- You were the one to go.
- My parents. I remembered them.

241
00:13:51.123 --> 00:13:52.543
What? What did you remember?

242
00:13:52.708 --> 00:13:54.788
I remembered them! My mom. My dad.

243
00:13:54.961 --> 00:13:58.801
I have a family. Oh! They don't know
where I am. Let's go. We have to go.

244
00:13:58.965 --> 00:14:02.385
Dory, no. No! This is crazy!
Where exactly are you trying to go?

245
00:14:02.551 --> 00:14:05.011
To the Gem of the Baltic?

246
00:14:05.179 --> 00:14:07.509
- The Jewel of Morro Bay, California.
- Yes!

247
00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:09.770
No, Dory. California's all the way
across the ocean.

248
00:14:09.892 --> 00:14:10.953
Then we'd better get going.

249
00:14:10.977 --> 00:14:14.807
How come every time we're on the edge
of this reef, one of us is trying...

250
00:14:14.981 --> 00:14:17.651
to leave?
For once, can't we just enjoy the view?

251
00:14:17.817 --> 00:14:20.417
How can you be talking about the view
when I remembered my family?

252
00:14:20.528 --> 00:14:23.698
No! We've done our ocean travels.
That part of our lives is over.

253
00:14:23.864 --> 00:14:26.164
The only reason to travel
in the first place is so...

254
00:14:26.325 --> 00:14:28.553
- you don't have to travel ever again.
- Yeah, but I want to...

255
00:14:29.912 --> 00:14:31.792
- Dory, look...
- Please.

256
00:14:32.707 --> 00:14:37.327
All I know is that I miss them.

257
00:14:39.672 --> 00:14:42.762
I really, really miss them.
I didn't know what that felt like.

258
00:14:45.177 --> 00:14:46.507
Do you know what that feels like?

259
00:14:53.019 --> 00:14:55.689
Yes, I know what that feels like.

260
00:14:57.273 --> 00:15:02.943
I don't want to forget this.
Somewhere out there is my family.

261
00:15:05.781 --> 00:15:09.281
Please, Marlin,
I can't find them on my own.

262
00:15:09.452 --> 00:15:12.702
I'll forget.
Please help me find my family.

263
00:15:12.872 --> 00:15:16.462
Yeah, Dad, you can get us all the way
across the ocean. Right?

264
00:15:17.376 --> 00:15:18.376
No.

265
00:15:21.756 --> 00:15:23.636
But I know a guy.

266
00:15:26.052 --> 00:15:27.237
Whoo-hoo!

267
00:15:27.261 --> 00:15:30.851
Righteous, righteous, righteous!

268
00:15:48.365 --> 00:15:52.535
Totally sick. Totally sick.

269
00:15:52.703 --> 00:15:54.123
I know. Isn't it great?

270
00:15:54.288 --> 00:15:56.618
No! I'm gonna be totally sick.

271
00:15:56.791 --> 00:15:59.581
It's the California current, dude.
It's got some gnarly chop.

272
00:15:59.752 --> 00:16:01.212
Surf's up, dude!

273
00:16:02.797 --> 00:16:05.257
Hey, dude, if you're gonna hurl,
just do me a solid...

274
00:16:05.424 --> 00:16:08.474
head to the back of the shell,
lean out, and go for distance.

275
00:16:08.636 --> 00:16:10.646
We call that "feeding the fishes."

276
00:16:10.805 --> 00:16:11.975
Correctamundo, Squirt!

277
00:16:12.139 --> 00:16:16.019
And now we're looking for my parents
at the Brooch of the Atlantic? Or the...

278
00:16:16.102 --> 00:16:18.192
- The Jewel of Morro Bay, California.
- Exactly!

279
00:16:18.270 --> 00:16:19.730
How are you gonna find your parents?

280
00:16:19.897 --> 00:16:21.687
Do you remember what they look like?

281
00:16:21.816 --> 00:16:23.710
I'm a bit new to the memory thing,
so I can't say for sure...

282
00:16:23.734 --> 00:16:27.444
but something tells me they were
mostly blue, with s... Maybe yellow.

283
00:16:27.613 --> 00:16:28.283
That sounds right.

284
00:16:28.447 --> 00:16:32.027
Also I'm pretty sure I'm gonna know
them when I see them. We're family.

285
00:16:32.159 --> 00:16:34.909
By the way crossing the ocean
is the kind of thing you should...

286
00:16:35.079 --> 00:16:37.079
only do once. One time!

287
00:16:37.248 --> 00:16:39.668
Morro Bay, California's
coming up, dudes.

288
00:16:40.793 --> 00:16:42.963
Whoo-hoo!
Let's find my family.

289
00:16:43.129 --> 00:16:44.289
Go! Go! Go, go, go.

290
00:16:44.463 --> 00:16:46.713
Just go, Dad.
Don't push me, Nemo.

291
00:16:50.261 --> 00:16:52.181
Whoo-hoo!

292
00:16:52.263 --> 00:16:55.643
So long, Little Blue!
Hope you find your parents.

293
00:16:55.808 --> 00:16:57.638
And good luck
"feeding the fishes."

294
00:16:58.936 --> 00:17:00.646
Too late. Already fed.

295
00:17:01.021 --> 00:17:02.021
Oh.

296
00:17:06.193 --> 00:17:09.493
This feels familiar. Mom! Dad!

297
00:17:09.655 --> 00:17:11.415
No. Dory! Dory! Wait! Wait.

298
00:17:12.158 --> 00:17:13.988
Mom! Dad!

299
00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:16.805
Stop yelling for a second.
Do you really think your parents...

300
00:17:16.829 --> 00:17:19.289
are just gonna be floating around here
waiting for you?

301
00:17:19.456 --> 00:17:22.716
Well, I don't know, but there's only
one way to find out. Mom! Dad!

302
00:17:22.877 --> 00:17:25.497
- Yell louder, Dory.
- Mom! Dad!

303
00:17:25.671 --> 00:17:27.381
- Sh!
- What was that?

304
00:17:28.007 --> 00:17:32.797
Wait. I've heard that before.
I remember someone saying, "Sh."

305
00:17:32.970 --> 00:17:34.930
Yes, well done. That was me.
One minute ago.

306
00:17:35.014 --> 00:17:35.684
Sh!

307
00:17:37.641 --> 00:17:40.731
Please. Have you seen
my mommy and daddy?

308
00:17:40.895 --> 00:17:43.155
Their names are Jenny and Charlie.

309
00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:44.230
Sh!

310
00:17:45.316 --> 00:17:47.946
Jenny and Charlie.

311
00:17:48.068 --> 00:17:48.898
What? Jenny and what?

312
00:17:48.986 --> 00:17:51.906
Those are their names!
My parents are Jenny and Charlie!

313
00:17:52.072 --> 00:17:53.612
- Dory, wait!
- Jenny!

314
00:17:53.699 --> 00:17:56.029
Can't we just take
a moment to come up with a plan?

315
00:17:56.202 --> 00:17:58.492
- Jenny! Charlie!
- Sh!

316
00:17:58.662 --> 00:18:00.872
- Are you crazy?
- Sorry, she's a little excited.

317
00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:03.750
- Jenny! Charlie!
- Dory, stop yelling for a second.

318
00:18:03.876 --> 00:18:06.546
It's not a good idea
to come into a new neighbourhood...

319
00:18:06.712 --> 00:18:09.092
and call this much attention to yourself.

320
00:18:09.256 --> 00:18:12.226
You don't understand. I remembered
my parent's names! Jenny! Charlie!

321
00:18:12.384 --> 00:18:16.054
These crabs are locals and I
get the feeling they're shushing...

322
00:18:16.222 --> 00:18:18.892
us for a reason. You might wake up
something dangerous.

323
00:18:19.016 --> 00:18:21.216
Are you talking about like
something with one big eye...

324
00:18:21.268 --> 00:18:22.138
tentacles, and a snappy thing?

325
00:18:22.269 --> 00:18:24.899
Well, that's very specific,
but something like that, yes.

326
00:18:25.064 --> 00:18:27.064
You just in general don't want to...

327
00:18:29.610 --> 00:18:32.610
Oh my goodness. Okay.

328
00:18:32.780 --> 00:18:37.240
There's a mistake. We're backing away.
Let us live and we will...

329
00:18:37.409 --> 00:18:41.909
We'll worship you. We'll build a...
Do you like a monument?

330
00:18:49.797 --> 00:18:54.337
Oh! Ooh! Whoa!
Swim for your life!

331
00:19:11.777 --> 00:19:13.397
- Nemo!
- Nemo!

332
00:19:14.905 --> 00:19:15.365
Dad!

333
00:19:15.489 --> 00:19:16.569
- Nemo!
- Dad!

334
00:19:22.788 --> 00:19:23.788
No!

335
00:19:23.956 --> 00:19:26.296
Nemo, hold on to me and don't let go!

336
00:19:27.126 --> 00:19:28.126
Dad!

337
00:19:28.419 --> 00:19:29.419
No, no! No!

338
00:19:35.676 --> 00:19:38.266
Dory! Dory, slow down!
We're not being chased any more.

339
00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:39.470
Are you sure?

340
00:19:43.309 --> 00:19:46.479
Jenny and Charlie. Jenny and Charlie!

341
00:19:47.271 --> 00:19:50.151
I just remembered their names!
We have to keep going. We're so close.

342
00:19:50.316 --> 00:19:51.446
- Huh?
- Nemo, are you hurt?

343
00:19:51.567 --> 00:19:55.147
Oh my goodness! Nemo!
Are you okay? What happened?

344
00:19:55.321 --> 00:19:56.991
- Not now, Dory. Please!
- Oh no.

345
00:19:57.156 --> 00:19:59.496
- Nemo. Oh no. Oh no.
- I'm okay.

346
00:19:59.658 --> 00:20:01.618
Oh, Nemo. I'm sorry. Okay. I'm sorry.

347
00:20:02.995 --> 00:20:05.005
Oh my goodness! Nemo, are you okay?

348
00:20:05.164 --> 00:20:07.124
I said, "Not now." You've done enough.

349
00:20:07.291 --> 00:20:12.541
I have? Oh no. But I can fix it.
I can. I'll go get help.

350
00:20:12.713 --> 00:20:15.173
You know what you can do, Dory?
You can go wait over there.

351
00:20:15.341 --> 00:20:18.931
Go wait over there and forget.
It's what you do best.

352
00:20:21.472 --> 00:20:24.512
You're right. I don't know why I thought
I could do this.

353
00:20:24.683 --> 00:20:29.063
Find my family. I can't do this.
I'm so sorry. I'll fix it.

354
00:20:29.229 --> 00:20:31.124
- I'm okay.
- Well, I'm gonna get help. Okay?

355
00:20:31.148 --> 00:20:35.188
Okay? I can do that. I'll be...
It'll be all right, Nemo.

356
00:20:38.322 --> 00:20:40.702
Hello? Someone? Hello?

357
00:20:40.866 --> 00:20:43.746
Anyone? Hello? Anyone?

358
00:20:43.911 --> 00:20:45.371
Hello.

359
00:20:46.538 --> 00:20:48.908
- Hello?
- I'm Sigourney Weaver.

360
00:20:49.083 --> 00:20:51.923
Oh. Hi, Sigourney. I need your help.

361
00:20:52.044 --> 00:20:54.044
Won't you please join us...

362
00:20:54.171 --> 00:20:55.591
Oh. Great, great, great.

363
00:20:55.756 --> 00:20:59.016
As we explore the wonders
of the Pacific Ocean...

364
00:20:59.176 --> 00:21:02.436
and the amazing life it holds within.

365
00:21:02.596 --> 00:21:04.766
Witness the majesty
of the Beluga Whale.

366
00:21:04.932 --> 00:21:06.392
Sigourney Weaver, where are you?

367
00:21:06.517 --> 00:21:07.557
Dory! There you are!

368
00:21:07.726 --> 00:21:10.396
Guys! I found help. Sigourney Weaver's
gonna tell us where we are.

369
00:21:10.562 --> 00:21:11.732
Look out!

370
00:21:11.897 --> 00:21:14.557
- Oh, look at this!
- No respect for ocean life.

371
00:21:14.691 --> 00:21:16.901
- Marlin! Nemo!
- Dory!

372
00:21:17.027 --> 00:21:18.213
No, no, no. Not again! Not again!

373
00:21:18.237 --> 00:21:19.881
Let's take her inside
and see how she does.

374
00:21:22.741 --> 00:21:23.411
Dory! Dory!

375
00:21:23.575 --> 00:21:27.245
Don't worry, Dory! Stay calm.
We'll come find you!

376
00:21:27.412 --> 00:21:29.912
And welcome to
the Marine Life Institute...

377
00:21:30.082 --> 00:21:34.292
where we believe in Rescue,
Rehabilitation and Release.

378
00:21:36.547 --> 00:21:38.087
Marlin? Nemo?

379
00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:46.220
Hello? Hello? Can you help me?

380
00:21:46.390 --> 00:21:48.220
Me help you?

381
00:21:48.475 --> 00:21:49.935
Ugh.

382
00:21:51.937 --> 00:21:52.937
Oh.

383
00:21:56.233 --> 00:21:58.403
Huh? What's happening? Help?

384
00:21:58.569 --> 00:21:59.849
Looks like we're done here.

385
00:21:59.903 --> 00:22:02.298
Dude, cut it out.
You're a scientist. We talked about this.

386
00:22:02.322 --> 00:22:03.662
Oh, come on. It's funny.

387
00:22:09.788 --> 00:22:12.498
Oh boy. Okay. This is...

388
00:22:12.583 --> 00:22:14.923
I'll be fine, I just need to find
a way out and...

389
00:22:24.011 --> 00:22:25.841
If I could just... Get a hold of yourself,

390
00:22:25.971 --> 00:22:27.115
get a hold of yourself.

391
00:22:27.139 --> 00:22:29.969
You'll be fine, everything's fine,
think positively.

392
00:22:30.142 --> 00:22:31.892
- Hey, you.
- Oh.

393
00:22:32.019 --> 00:22:32.849
Spinner.

394
00:22:33.020 --> 00:22:35.480
Oh, thank goodness. Hi, I'm Dory. I'm...

395
00:22:35.606 --> 00:22:37.526
Name's Hank. How sick are you?

396
00:22:37.691 --> 00:22:38.821
Sick? I'm sick?

397
00:22:38.984 --> 00:22:40.128
Why else would you be in quarantine?

398
00:22:40.152 --> 00:22:42.192
Oh no! How long do I have?
I have to find my family.

399
00:22:42.237 --> 00:22:44.857
All right. Now don't get hysterical...
Uh-oh. Not good.

400
00:22:45.032 --> 00:22:47.662
What? What is it? What happened?
What's that?

401
00:22:47.826 --> 00:22:49.376
That there is bad news.

402
00:22:49.661 --> 00:22:52.871
It's a transport tag for fish
who can't cut it inside the institute.

403
00:22:53.040 --> 00:22:56.170
They get transferred to permanent digs.
An aquarium.

404
00:22:56.335 --> 00:22:57.925
In Cleveland.

405
00:22:58.462 --> 00:23:03.222
Fish in here, go back in the ocean.
Cleveland fish, stay there forever.

406
00:23:03.634 --> 00:23:05.974
Cleveland? No!
I can't go to the Cleveland.

407
00:23:06.136 --> 00:23:08.976
I have to get to the Jewel of Morro Bay,
California and find my family.

408
00:23:09.139 --> 00:23:10.969
That's this place.
The Marine Life Institute.

409
00:23:11.099 --> 00:23:13.889
The Jewel of Morro Bay, California.
You're here.

410
00:23:14.686 --> 00:23:15.196
You mean I'm from here?

411
00:23:15.228 --> 00:23:17.688
My parents are here.
I have to get to them.

412
00:23:17.856 --> 00:23:19.066
So what exhibit are you from?

413
00:23:19.232 --> 00:23:22.192
Wait. I'm from an exhibit?
Which one? I have to get there.

414
00:23:22.361 --> 00:23:24.491
Hmm. That's a hard one, kid.

415
00:23:24.655 --> 00:23:28.825
Unless... Nah.
Never work. It's too crazy.

416
00:23:28.951 --> 00:23:30.991
What do you mean? Just tell me.
I'm okay with crazy.

417
00:23:31.119 --> 00:23:34.159
You know, I could see that?
Well, there's one thing I can think of...

418
00:23:34.331 --> 00:23:37.251
to help you get to your family.
If I just take...

419
00:23:37.417 --> 00:23:39.497
Yes! Great idea.
You take me to find them.

420
00:23:39.586 --> 00:23:40.676
Why didn't I think of that?

421
00:23:40.837 --> 00:23:43.707
Uh, no, no, no.
If I just take your tag...

422
00:23:43.882 --> 00:23:47.552
I can take your place on the transport
truck then you can go back inside...

423
00:23:47.719 --> 00:23:50.889
and find your family.
All you have to do is give me the tag.

424
00:23:51.056 --> 00:23:53.106
What tag?
There's a tag on my fin!

425
00:23:53.225 --> 00:23:55.685
How could you forget
you have a tag on your fin?

426
00:23:55.811 --> 00:23:59.731
Oh no. I'm sorry. I...
I suffer from short-term memory loss.

427
00:24:00.565 --> 00:24:02.251
You don't remember
what we were talking about?

428
00:24:02.275 --> 00:24:04.945
Mm-mm. Not a clue.
What were we talking about?

429
00:24:05.070 --> 00:24:07.900
Um, you were about to give me your tag.

430
00:24:08.073 --> 00:24:10.203
Well, I kind of like my tag.
Why do you want it?

431
00:24:10.325 --> 00:24:11.325
So I can go to...

432
00:24:12.661 --> 00:24:14.371
So I can go to Cleveland.

433
00:24:14.538 --> 00:24:15.682
Cleveland? Mmm.
I hear good things

434
00:24:15.706 --> 00:24:16.975
about Cleveland.
Why do you want to go?

435
00:24:16.999 --> 00:24:19.352
Because if I stay here I'm gonna get
released back to the ocean.

436
00:24:19.376 --> 00:24:21.546
And I have extremely
unpleasant memories of that place.

437
00:24:23.213 --> 00:24:25.303
I just want to live in a glass box alone.

438
00:24:25.465 --> 00:24:28.095
That's all I want. So give me your tag!

439
00:24:28.260 --> 00:24:29.590
Hey, man, don't touch my tag!

440
00:24:32.764 --> 00:24:33.764
Look...

441
00:24:39.938 --> 00:24:42.938
I don't work here.
It's not like I have a map of this place.

442
00:24:43.108 --> 00:24:44.318
A map! Good idea.

443
00:24:44.484 --> 00:24:47.534
You take me to the map, I figure out
where my parents are. Oh boy.

444
00:24:48.488 --> 00:24:52.158
All right. If I get you to your family
will you give me...

445
00:24:52.284 --> 00:24:55.914
I don't have much. Um, I...
How about if I give you this tag?

446
00:24:56.997 --> 00:24:58.407
Great idea.

447
00:25:04.671 --> 00:25:06.671
Are you absolutely
sure that's what I said?

448
00:25:06.840 --> 00:25:09.630
"Go wait over there and forget.
That's what you do best."

449
00:25:09.801 --> 00:25:10.841
- Yeah, Dad.
- I said that?

450
00:25:10.969 --> 00:25:12.759
You said that, Dory swam to the surface,

451
00:25:12.846 --> 00:25:14.146
and she got taken by some...

452
00:25:14.306 --> 00:25:15.575
All right, I don't want to hear
the whole story again.

453
00:25:15.599 --> 00:25:18.809
I was just asking about the one part
because, look, if I said that...

454
00:25:18.977 --> 00:25:22.807
I'm not positive I did.
It's actually a compliment because...

455
00:25:22.981 --> 00:25:25.981
I asked her to wait and I said,
"It's what you do best."

456
00:25:26.151 --> 00:25:29.151
So I... Oh, it's my fault!

457
00:25:29.321 --> 00:25:33.161
It's all my fault she got kidnapped
and taken into whatever this place is.

458
00:25:33.325 --> 00:25:34.955
What if it's a restaurant?

459
00:25:35.118 --> 00:25:37.448
Oy! You two! Shut it!

460
00:25:37.621 --> 00:25:41.461
Yeah, we're trying to sleep!
You interrupted my favourite dream!

461
00:25:41.625 --> 00:25:43.425
Is that the one about you
laying on this rock?

462
00:25:43.502 --> 00:25:45.842
- Yeah.
- Oh, that is a good one.

463
00:25:46.004 --> 00:25:47.815
- Oh yeah, isn't it? Yeah.
- It's one of my favourites.

464
00:25:47.839 --> 00:25:48.509
Uh, excuse us. Hello!

465
00:25:48.590 --> 00:25:49.830
- Son! Son.
- We're trying to...

466
00:25:50.175 --> 00:25:52.685
Those are sea lions.
They are natural predators.

467
00:25:52.844 --> 00:25:54.124
They could pounce at any moment.

468
00:25:55.931 --> 00:25:57.641
Uh, they don't look very pouncy.

469
00:25:57.808 --> 00:25:59.348
That's what they want you to think.

470
00:25:59.518 --> 00:26:02.188
Just get behind me
and let me do the talking.

471
00:26:02.354 --> 00:26:05.774
Excuse me, we're worried
about our friend. Is that a restaurant?

472
00:26:07.234 --> 00:26:10.694
Mate, it's not a restaurant.
Your friend is okay.

473
00:26:10.862 --> 00:26:12.992
- She is?
- It's a fish hospital.

474
00:26:13.156 --> 00:26:17.416
Sigourney Weaver says she'll be
rescued, rehabilitated, and released.

475
00:26:17.577 --> 00:26:19.577
She'll be in and out in a jiff.
We should know.

476
00:26:19.746 --> 00:26:21.336
- Nasal parasite.
- Anaemia.

477
00:26:21.498 --> 00:26:23.078
All fixed up and sent on our way.

478
00:26:23.208 --> 00:26:25.288
Oh thank goodness.

479
00:26:25.418 --> 00:26:28.418
Sure, that's all right.
Don't you worry ab...

480
00:26:29.506 --> 00:26:31.818
- Gerald, get off the rock!
- Shove off, Gerald! Come on. Off! Off!

481
00:26:31.842 --> 00:26:35.722
- Get off! Now you know better! Off!
- Off! Off! Off! Off!

482
00:26:35.887 --> 00:26:40.717
Don't you worry about a thing.
That place is the Marine Life Institute.

483
00:26:40.892 --> 00:26:42.982
The Jewel of Morro Bay, California.

484
00:26:43.103 --> 00:26:44.983
She was right.

485
00:26:45.063 --> 00:26:47.233
It looks like Dory
can do something besides forget.

486
00:26:47.399 --> 00:26:49.189
Thank you, Nemo. Thank you for that.

487
00:26:49.359 --> 00:26:51.399
So how are we gonna get inside?

488
00:26:51.528 --> 00:26:53.068
Wait. You want to get inside MLI?

489
00:26:53.238 --> 00:26:55.908
Desperately. Our friend is in there.
Lost, alone.

490
00:26:56.074 --> 00:26:58.244
She's scared.
She'll have no idea what to do.

491
00:26:58.410 --> 00:27:01.450
Oh, we know a way.

492
00:27:01.580 --> 00:27:02.750
You do?

493
00:27:02.873 --> 00:27:05.293
Ooo-roo.
Ooo-roo-roo. Ooo-roo.

494
00:27:05.417 --> 00:27:08.247
- What are they doing?
- I don't know. It sounds bad.

495
00:27:09.754 --> 00:27:11.524
Are we there yet?
Sh. Keep it down!

496
00:27:11.548 --> 00:27:15.338
Hank, I'm so glad I found you.
It feels like... I... Destiny.

497
00:27:15.594 --> 00:27:18.394
For what must be the millionth time,
it's not destiny.

498
00:27:18.555 --> 00:27:20.815
Uh-oh. Have I said "destiny" before?
I'm sorry.

499
00:27:20.974 --> 00:27:23.094
I'm just so nervous
because I'm gonna meet my parents.

500
00:27:23.226 --> 00:27:25.580
I haven't seen them in I don't even know
how long because...

501
00:27:25.604 --> 00:27:27.915
- you see I suffer from short-term...
- Short-term memory loss.

502
00:27:27.939 --> 00:27:29.709
Look, no more talking. Okay?
I don't like talking.

503
00:27:29.733 --> 00:27:32.253
I don't like chatter and questions.
And, "How are you? Oh I'm fine."

504
00:27:33.320 --> 00:27:35.480
"How are you? I'm fine too."
News flash -nobody's fine.

505
00:27:35.614 --> 00:27:36.404
Oh, I'm fine. How are you?

506
00:27:37.657 --> 00:27:39.657
- Hank, look, there's a map!
- Sh!

507
00:27:39.784 --> 00:27:42.597
The plan is you're gonna read that
and figure out where your parents live.

508
00:27:42.621 --> 00:27:44.461
Then I'm on the truck to Cleveland.
You got it?

509
00:27:44.623 --> 00:27:46.793
Got it. What was the first part again?

510
00:27:46.958 --> 00:27:48.248
Ugh.

511
00:27:48.376 --> 00:27:49.562
What? The octopus escaped again?

512
00:27:49.586 --> 00:27:52.176
Wow. Look at all the exhibits.

513
00:27:52.297 --> 00:27:54.297
How can you do this park in one day?
Seriously.

514
00:27:54.466 --> 00:27:55.766
- Pick one!
- Okay. Um...

515
00:27:56.801 --> 00:27:58.613
Well,
tell everyone to keep an eye out.

516
00:27:58.637 --> 00:28:02.257
We're supposed to be releasing
the octopus back to the ocean today.

517
00:28:04.809 --> 00:28:07.639
Well, of course I haven't seen him.
If I was looking I'd find him.

518
00:28:07.812 --> 00:28:09.732
Hank! There you are.

519
00:28:09.856 --> 00:28:11.366
- Hurry up!
- Okay. Okay.

520
00:28:11.524 --> 00:28:16.784
K. It starts with a "k."
Kid z-own-y. Kid zone!

521
00:28:16.947 --> 00:28:18.857
No! No kids. Kids grab things.

522
00:28:18.949 --> 00:28:20.819
And I'm not losing
another tentacle for you.

523
00:28:20.992 --> 00:28:23.532
You lost a tentacle?
Well then you're not an octopus,

524
00:28:23.620 --> 00:28:24.870
you're a septopus.

525
00:28:25.038 --> 00:28:26.478
I may not remember, but I can count.

526
00:28:26.539 --> 00:28:27.829
- Hurry up!
- Okay.

527
00:28:27.958 --> 00:28:31.418
Journey to the... Hey, look. Shells.

528
00:28:34.005 --> 00:28:35.425
Hey, look. Shells!

529
00:28:36.883 --> 00:28:38.513
Daddy, here's a shell for you.

530
00:28:38.677 --> 00:28:41.177
That's great, Dory.
You found another one.

531
00:28:41.346 --> 00:28:43.396
- I did?
- Oh, yes, you did.

532
00:28:43.556 --> 00:28:44.976
You're getting good at this, Dory.

533
00:28:48.144 --> 00:28:49.524
Hey, look. Shells!

534
00:28:51.022 --> 00:28:54.112
- Hey, I live there.
- Yes! Yes, indeed.

535
00:28:54.234 --> 00:28:57.534
- I like shells.
- That's right, dear.

536
00:28:59.197 --> 00:29:01.357
Do you think you could find me
another shell?

537
00:29:02.075 --> 00:29:03.705
Purple ones
are my favourite.

538
00:29:05.829 --> 00:29:07.199
Okay, Mommy.

539
00:29:08.873 --> 00:29:11.673
Mommy. Purple shell. Purple shell!
Hey, my home had a purple shell.

540
00:29:14.087 --> 00:29:16.357
So what? Half the exhibits here
have purple shells in them.

541
00:29:16.381 --> 00:29:18.359
No, no, no. You don't understand.
I remember her now.

542
00:29:18.383 --> 00:29:20.983
Purple shells were her favourite
and she had this adorable giggle.

543
00:29:21.094 --> 00:29:22.488
And then my dad was really friendly.

544
00:29:22.512 --> 00:29:24.392
And now your wacky memory's
gonna get us caught.
